IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `la-dates`
IMPORT `la-core`
IMPORT `la-seat`

-- Limitation Act 1969 (NSW) -- cases for the seat of the person bringing the claim (la-seat.l4). Every expected value
-- was worked by hand from the deposited text (the section is named on each group), never copied from the encoding's
-- output; day counts are shown where they matter (checked with a calendar, independently of the encoding). Edges: the
-- 18th birthday and the day before, 29 February, 6 December 2002 and the day before, 1 September 1990 and the day
-- before, "from and including" against "from", the 28-day incapacity and 27 days, an incapacity beginning on the last
-- day and the day after, the 3-years-before-death edge of s 50C(2)(a), the 30-year ultimate bar, the s 62D year after
-- the 18th birthday to the day, and the s 62A cap against the 3-year period.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases: the person bringing the claim`

`ANY` MEANS `the date` 1 1 2000
`PI` MEANS `damages for death or personal injury`
`SELF` MEANS `the person injured or wronged, suing for themselves`
`ESTATE` MEANS `the personal representative of the injured person, who has died, suing for the estate (a survivor action)`
`RELS` MEANS `relatives suing for the death (a compensation to relatives action)`
`NOABUSE` MEANS `the injury did not result from abuse`
`CONTRACT` MEANS `damages or money in contract (not under a deed) or tort with no personal injury, or money recoverable under an enactment`
`DEED` MEANS `a claim founded on a deed`
`JUDG` MEANS `a claim on a judgment`
`PENALTY` MEANS `a penalty or forfeiture recoverable under an enactment`
`OTHERACT` MEANS `a claim for which another Act fixes the limitation period, such as a motor accident claim`
`OTHERKIND` MEANS `another kind of claim`
`CONN18` MEANS `other abuse connected with sexual or serious physical abuse of me, which was also perpetrated before I turned 18`
`CONNADULT` MEANS `other abuse connected with sexual or serious physical abuse of me, which was perpetrated when I was 18 or older`

`YES6A` MEANS `yes, no time limit: an action for damages for death or personal injury resulting from child abuse may be brought at any time and is not subject to any limitation period under this Act (s 6A(1)); the court keeps its powers, for example to dismiss or stay proceedings where a fair trial is no longer possible (s 6A(6))`
`NO18` MEANS `no: child abuse is abuse perpetrated against you when you were under 18 years of age (s 6A(2)), and this abuse was not`
`NOCONN` MEANS `no: connected abuse is child abuse only if the sexual or serious physical abuse it was connected with was also perpetrated when you were under 18 (s 6A(3))`
`NOLIST` MEANS `no: child abuse means sexual abuse, serious physical abuse, or other abuse connected with either (s 6A(2)), and this abuse is none of them`
`NOABUSEANS` MEANS `no: s 6A applies only to damages for death or personal injury resulting from child abuse, and this injury did not result from abuse (s 6A(1))`
`NOPI` MEANS `no: s 6A covers only an action for damages that relates to death or personal injury (s 6A(1))`

`CL9A` MEANS `yes: s 6A applies to a cause of action that arose before s 6A commenced, whether or not a limitation period had already expired (Sch 5 cl 9(a))`
`CL9B` MEANS `yes: s 6A applies whether or not an action was commenced previously on the claim (Sch 5 cl 9(b))`
`CL10` MEANS `yes: you may bring the action as if the earlier action had not been commenced; the court hearing it may, if it decides it is just and reasonable, set aside the earlier judgment and take into account damages and costs paid or payable under it (Sch 5 cll 8(2), 9, 10); only the Supreme Court may set aside another court's judgment`
`SETTLED` MEANS `the Act does not say: Schedule 5 deals with judgments and with agreements made in connection with a judgment (cl 8(2)), not with a settlement made without one`
`NOHELP5` MEANS `no: s 6A does not apply to the claim on these facts, so Schedule 5 Part 3 does not help`

`PNONE` MEANS `none: an action for child abuse may be brought at any time (s 6A)`
`PDIV6` MEANS `the first to expire of 3 years running from and including the day the claim is discoverable, and 12 years running from the act or omission (s 50C(1))`
`P50E` MEANS `the first to expire of 3 years from the day the claim is discoverable, which is no earlier than the victim's 25th birthday, and 12 years running from that birthday (s 50C(1), s 50E)`
`PRELS` MEANS `the first to expire of 3 years from the day the claim is discoverable, which is no earlier than the death, and 12 years running from the death (s 50C(1), (3), s 50D(4))`
`PSURV` MEANS `the first to expire of 3 years from the day the claim is discoverable as s 50C(2) works it out for a survivor action, and 12 years running from the act or omission (s 50C(1), (2))`
`P18A` MEANS `3 years running from the day the cause of action accrued (s 18A)`
`P19B` MEANS `3 years running from the death (s 19(1)(b))`
`P19A` MEANS `6 years running from the death (s 19(1)(a))`
`P14` MEANS `6 years running from the day the cause of action accrued (s 14)`
`P16` MEANS `12 years running from the day the cause of action accrued (s 16)`
`P17` MEANS `12 years running from the day the judgment became enforceable (s 17)`
`P18` MEANS `2 years running from the day the cause of action accrued (s 18)`
`P7` MEANS `no: nothing in this Act applies where another Act fixes the limitation period (s 7(a); for a motor accident claim also s 50A(3))`
`PNC1990` MEANS `not covered: a personal injury claim that accrued before 1 September 1990 (Part 3 Division 3 Subdivision 1)`
`PNCKIND` MEANS `not covered: a kind of claim this encoding does not cover`

`NOLAST` MEANS `there is no last day: an action for child abuse may be brought at any time (s 6A)`
`LAST7` MEANS `this Act does not fix the time: another Act fixes the limitation period (s 7(a))`
`LASTNC` MEANS `not covered by this encoding`

`INTIME` MEANS `in time: it was brought on or before the last day`
`LATE` MEANS `late: it was brought after the last day`
`STILL` MEANS `still in time: it has not been brought yet and the last day has not passed`
`LATENOT` MEANS `late: it has not been brought and the last day has passed`
`INTIME6A` MEANS `in time: there is no limitation period for an action for child abuse (s 6A)`
`T7` MEANS `this Act does not say: another Act fixes the limitation period (s 7(a))`
`TNC` MEANS `not covered: the time limit for this kind of claim is not worked out here`

`NOTDIV6` MEANS `s 50D does not reach this: discoverability sets the time only for a personal injury claim under Division 6`

`NOTJR` MEANS `not on these facts: the court may extend only if it decides that it is just and reasonable to do so (s 62A(2))`
`NOHELP62A` MEANS `no help: the 3-year post-discoverability period ends no later than the long-stop, and s 62A extends only the long-stop`
`NOREACH62A` MEANS `s 62A does not reach this: it extends only the 12-year long-stop of a personal injury claim under Division 6`

`YES62D` MEANS `yes, if the court so orders: the limitation period may be extended to expire one year after the court's order (s 62D(2))`
`NOTFACTS62D` MEANS `not on these facts: the court may extend only if your parent's or guardian's irrational decision, made while you were a minor, caused the failure to sue, and there is evidence to establish the claim (s 62D(2)(b), (c))`
`NOTMINOR62D` MEANS `no: s 62D is only for a person who was a minor at the time of the act or omission (s 62D(1))`
`NOTWITHIN62D` MEANS `no: s 62D reaches only a limitation period that expired before, or within 1 year after, you turned 18 (s 62D(2)(a))`
`NOREACH62D` MEANS `s 62D does not reach this: it is for the injured person's own claim under Division 6`

`E6A` MEANS `nothing expires: there is no limitation period for an action for child abuse (s 6A)`
`EDIV6` MEANS `when the period expires your right to the damages is extinguished as against the defendant and their successors, unless you brought your action before then (s 63(1), (2)); a court may still extend the period under Part 3 Division 4, and the expiry then has no effect (s 62F)`
`EMONEY` MEANS `when the period expires your right to the money is extinguished as against the defendant and their successors, unless you brought your action before then (s 63(1), (2))`
`E7` MEANS `this Act does not say what happens: another Act fixes the limitation period (s 7(a))`
`ENC` MEANS `not covered: what happens is not worked out here for this kind of claim`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Last day answer`
`LASTON` d m y MEANS `the last day to commence the action is` (`the date` d m y)

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Last day answer`
`STOPPEDTO` d m y MEANS `the time is stopped while your incapacity continues (s 50F, s 52), but the action is barred after` (`the date` d m y)

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Discoverable answer`
`DISCON` d m y MEANS `your claim counts as discoverable from` (`the date` d m y)

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Long-stop extension answer`
`EXTTO` d m y MEANS `yes, if the court decides it is just and reasonable: the court may extend the 12-year long-stop, and the last day you could then commence is` (`the date` d m y)

-- s 6A(1), (2), (3). Born 1 March 1980: the 18th birthday is 1 March 1998.
#ASSERT `Is there a time limit on my child abuse claim` `sexual abuse` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 1980) (`the date` 1 3 1990) EQUALS `YES6A`
#ASSERT `Is there a time limit on my child abuse claim` `serious physical abuse` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 1980) (`the date` 28 2 1998) EQUALS `YES6A`
#ASSERT `Is there a time limit on my child abuse claim` `sexual abuse` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 1980) (`the date` 1 3 1998) EQUALS `NO18`
#ASSERT `Is there a time limit on my child abuse claim` `CONN18` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 1980) (`the date` 1 3 1992) EQUALS `YES6A`
#ASSERT `Is there a time limit on my child abuse claim` `CONNADULT` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 1980) (`the date` 1 3 1997) EQUALS `NOCONN`
#ASSERT `Is there a time limit on my child abuse claim` `CONNADULT` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 1980) (`the date` 1 3 1999) EQUALS `NO18`
#ASSERT `Is there a time limit on my child abuse claim` `physical abuse that was not serious, not connected with sexual or serious physical abuse` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 1980) (`the date` 1 3 1990) EQUALS `NOLIST`
#ASSERT `Is there a time limit on my child abuse claim` `other abuse not connected with sexual or serious physical abuse` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 1980) (`the date` 1 3 1990) EQUALS `NOLIST`
#ASSERT `Is there a time limit on my child abuse claim` `NOABUSE` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 1980) (`the date` 1 3 1990) EQUALS `NOABUSEANS`
#ASSERT `Is there a time limit on my child abuse claim` `sexual abuse` FALSE (`the date` 1 3 1980) (`the date` 1 3 1990) EQUALS `NOPI`
-- Born 29 February 2000: fork F1 puts the 18th birthday on 28 February 2018.
#ASSERT `Is there a time limit on my child abuse claim` `sexual abuse` TRUE (`the date` 29 2 2000) (`the date` 27 2 2018) EQUALS `YES6A`
#ASSERT `Is there a time limit on my child abuse claim` `sexual abuse` TRUE (`the date` 29 2 2000) (`the date` 28 2 2018) EQUALS `NO18`

-- Schedule 5 cll 8(2), 9, 10.
#ASSERT `Can I sue now on my child abuse claim that was barred or judged before` `sexual abuse` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 1980) (`the date` 1 3 1990) `there was no earlier action or judgment on the claim` EQUALS `CL9A`
#ASSERT `Can I sue now on my child abuse claim that was barred or judged before` `sexual abuse` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 1980) (`the date` 1 3 1990) `an earlier action was commenced, but no judgment was given on the ground that the limitation period had expired` EQUALS `CL9B`
#ASSERT `Can I sue now on my child abuse claim that was barred or judged before` `sexual abuse` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 1980) (`the date` 1 3 1990) `a judgment on the claim was given or entered on the ground that the limitation period had expired` EQUALS `CL10`
#ASSERT `Can I sue now on my child abuse claim that was barred or judged before` `serious physical abuse` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 1980) (`the date` 1 3 1990) `a judgment against my lawyers for professional negligence was given on the ground that a limitation period had expired` EQUALS `CL10`
#ASSERT `Can I sue now on my child abuse claim that was barred or judged before` `sexual abuse` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 1980) (`the date` 1 3 1990) `an agreement was made before and in connection with such a judgment` EQUALS `CL10`
#ASSERT `Can I sue now on my child abuse claim that was barred or judged before` `sexual abuse` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 1980) (`the date` 1 3 1990) `the claim was settled, with no judgment on the limitation ground` EQUALS `SETTLED`
#ASSERT `Can I sue now on my child abuse claim that was barred or judged before` `sexual abuse` TRUE (`the date` 1 3 1980) (`the date` 1 3 1999) `a judgment on the claim was given or entered on the ground that the limitation period had expired` EQUALS `NOHELP5`

-- Which period (s 6A, s 7, ss 14, 16-19, 50A-50E). Division 6 from 6 December 2002 (finding 1).
